## PART B — SALE AND PURCHASE

### 2. SALE AND PURCHASE

**2.1** Subject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement, the Seller agrees to sell, and the Buyer agrees to purchase, the Sale Shares with full title guarantee, free from all Encumbrances and together with all rights and benefits attaching to them at Completion (including all dividends and distributions declared, paid, or made after the Signing Date).

**2.2** The Seller waives, and shall procure the waiver of, any rights of pre-emption, rights of first refusal or similar rights in respect of the Sale Shares that may be conferred on any person under the constitutional documents of the Company, any shareholders' agreement, or otherwise.

**2.3** The Buyer shall not be required to complete the purchase of any of the Sale Shares unless the purchase of all of the Sale Shares is completed simultaneously.

**2.4** Title to and beneficial ownership of the Sale Shares shall pass to the Buyer at Completion.

### 3. INTERCONDITIONAL OBLIGATIONS

**3.1** This Agreement is not conditional (save as set out in Clause 4). The obligation to complete is subject only to the Conditions being satisfied or waived in accordance with Clause 4.

---

## PART C — CONDITIONS

### 4. CONDITIONS

**4.1** Completion is conditional on the following Conditions being satisfied or waived (in accordance with Clause 4.5) on or before the Long-Stop Date:

(a) *Merger Control / Regulatory Approvals:* receipt of all Regulatory Approvals set out in **Schedule 5** (*Required Consents and Approvals*) in form and substance reasonably satisfactory to the Buyer, without conditions or requirements that are, individually or in the aggregate, materially burdensome to the Buyer's Group or the Group;

(b) *No MAC:* no MAC having occurred between the Signing Date and the Completion Date; *[ISSUE-7]*;

(c) *Third-Party Consents:* receipt of all material third-party consents required in connection with the Transaction as listed in **Schedule 5**, including *[JV partner consent — ISSUE-4]*;

(d) *Financing:* *[TO BE DETERMINED — ISSUE-5: If Buyer is debt-financed, insert condition re: availability of committed financing. Delete if equity-funded.]*; and

(e) *No Order:* there being no injunction, order, or other restraint issued by any court or Government Authority of competent jurisdiction that prohibits or materially restricts the Transaction.

**4.2 Satisfaction of Conditions**

(a) The Parties shall use their respective reasonable endeavours to procure the satisfaction of the Conditions as promptly as reasonably practicable, and in any event before the Long-Stop Date.

(b) The Buyer shall: (i) file or cause to be filed all required notifications and applications with the relevant Government Authorities as soon as reasonably practicable after the Signing Date, and in any event within [10] Business Days thereof; (ii) use reasonable endeavours to obtain merger clearances and Regulatory Approvals at the earliest possible date; and (iii) not take any action that would, or would reasonably be expected to, materially delay or prevent the receipt of such clearances.

(c) The Seller shall provide all information reasonably requested by the Buyer or any Government Authority in connection with obtaining Regulatory Approvals.

**4.3 Notification**

Each Party shall promptly notify the other Party in writing upon becoming aware of: (i) any Condition having been satisfied; (ii) any event or circumstance that has occurred or is likely to occur which would result in any Condition becoming incapable of being satisfied; or (iii) any material development in relation to any Regulatory Approval.

**4.4 Long-Stop Date**

If any Condition has not been satisfied (or waived) on or before the Long-Stop Date, either Party may terminate this Agreement by written notice to the other Party without liability to either Party, except that: (i) any rights and liabilities which have accrued prior to such termination shall survive; and (ii) the provisions of Clauses 1 (*Definitions and Interpretation*), 21 (*Confidentiality*), 22 (*Announcements*), 25 (*Governing Law and Jurisdiction*), and this Clause 4.4 shall survive termination.

**4.5 Waiver of Conditions**

The Buyer may waive any Condition set out in Clause 4.1(b) to 4.1(e) (but not Clause 4.1(a)) by written notice to the Seller at any time before the Long-Stop Date. Any such waiver shall be unconditional.

