## PART F — COMPLETION

### 9. COMPLETION

**9.1** Completion shall take place on the Completion Date at the offices of [●], or at such other place as the Parties may agree in writing.

**9.2 Seller's obligations at Completion**

At Completion, the Seller shall deliver or procure the delivery to the Buyer of each of the following:

(a) duly executed instrument(s) of transfer of the Sale Shares in favour of the Buyer (or its nominee);

(b) the share certificate(s) representing the Sale Shares (or a duly executed indemnity in lieu of lost certificate(s) in the Agreed Form);

(c) a copy of the resolutions of the board of directors of the Company (in the Agreed Form): (i) approving the transfer of the Sale Shares; (ii) registering the Buyer (or its nominee) as the holder of the Sale Shares; and (iii) appointing such directors as the Buyer may nominate (and accepting the resignations of such directors as the Buyer requires);

(d) signed resignation letters from each resigning director and officer of each Group Company (in the Agreed Form), with effect from Completion;

(e) the Disclosure Letter, duly executed by the Seller;

(f) the Escrow Agreement, duly executed by the Seller;

(g) evidence of receipt of, or satisfaction of, each Condition;

(h) a certificate from the Seller (signed by a duly authorised director) confirming that: (i) the Fundamental Warranties are true and accurate in all material respects as at Completion; and (ii) the conduct of business undertakings in Clause 8 have been complied with in all material respects;

(i) the original statutory books and minute books of each Group Company, duly brought up to date;

(j) the common seal (if any) of each Group Company;

(k) all third-party consents and Regulatory Approvals listed in Schedule 5;

(l) evidence that all Related-Party Arrangements listed in **Schedule 8** (*Related Party Arrangements*) have been terminated or novated in accordance with Clause 10; and

(m) such other documents as may be required by applicable law or as the Buyer may reasonably request.

**9.3 Buyer's obligations at Completion**

At Completion, the Buyer shall:

(a) pay the Completion Payment to the Seller in accordance with Clause 7.1;

(b) pay the Escrow Amount into the Escrow Account in accordance with Clause 7.2;

(c) deliver the Escrow Agreement, duly executed by the Buyer; and

(d) deliver evidence of authorisation of the Buyer to enter into and perform its obligations under the Transaction Documents.

**9.4 Simultaneous obligations**

All actions at Completion are inter-conditional. No action shall be deemed to have been taken, and no document shall be deemed to have been delivered, until all actions have been taken and all documents have been delivered.

**9.5 Failure to Complete**

If the Seller or the Buyer fails to comply with any material obligation under this Clause 9 on the Completion Date:

(a) the complying Party shall be entitled (without prejudice to any other rights or remedies) to:

(i) proceed to Completion so far as practicable; or

(ii) fix a new Completion Date (not more than [10] Business Days after the original Completion Date); or

(iii) terminate this Agreement if the failure is not remedied within [5] Business Days of written notice from the complying Party;

and the exercise of any of the above options shall not limit or waive any claim for damages.

