## PART H — WARRANTIES

### 12. SELLER'S WARRANTIES

**12.1** The Seller warrants to the Buyer that each of the Warranties is true, accurate, and not misleading as at the Signing Date, and (where the Warranties are expressed to be given as at the Signing Date only) as at the Signing Date; and (where not so expressed) as at the Signing Date and as at Completion (in each case with reference to the facts and circumstances then subsisting).

**12.2** Each Warranty is to be construed independently and, except where expressly provided otherwise, no Warranty limits any other.

**12.3** The Warranties are qualified by: (i) matters fairly disclosed in the Disclosure Letter; (ii) matters fairly disclosed by the Data Room Documents; and (iii) matters disclosed in the Schedules to this Agreement (in each case to the extent the disclosure is sufficiently specific to put the Buyer on notice of the relevant matter). *[Note: extent of Data Room disclosure qualification to be negotiated — Buyer typically resists broad Data Room qualification.]*

**12.4** The Seller acknowledges that the Buyer has entered into this Agreement in reliance on the Warranties, the information contained in the Disclosure Letter and the Transaction Documents.

**12.5** The Warranties given at Completion shall be deemed to be repeated by the Seller as at Completion by reference to the facts and circumstances then existing.

**12.6** The Seller shall promptly notify the Buyer in writing (a "**Warranty Notification**") upon becoming aware of any matter, fact, or circumstance which constitutes, or is reasonably likely to constitute, a breach of any Warranty. Delivery of a Warranty Notification shall not relieve the Seller of any liability in respect of any such breach.

