(d) Any Claim (other than a Tax Claim) notified pursuant to paragraphs (a) or (b) above shall be deemed to have lapsed if proceedings in respect thereof have not been commenced (by service of process) within [12] months after the date of such notice.

**13.2 Financial Limits**

(a) *De minimis:* The Seller shall not be liable for any individual Claim where the liability does not exceed [●] ("**De Minimis Amount**"); provided that for the purposes of calculating the aggregate threshold, Claims below the De Minimis Amount shall be aggregated;

(b) *Threshold / Tipping Basket:* The Seller shall not be liable for any Claim unless the aggregate liability of all Claims exceeds [●] ("**Claim Threshold**"), in which case the Seller shall be liable for the full aggregate amount of all Claims (not merely the excess above the Threshold);

(c) *General Cap:* Subject to Clause 13.2(d), the Seller's aggregate liability for all Claims (excluding Fundamental Warranty Claims and Tax Claims) shall not exceed [●]% of the Consideration;

(d) *Fundamental Warranty Cap:* The Seller's aggregate liability for all Claims (including Fundamental Warranty Claims) shall not exceed [●]% of the Consideration; *[ISSUE-2: percentage to be agreed — Seller proposes 50%; Buyer proposes 100%; fallback 75%]*;

(e) *Tax Cap:* The Seller's aggregate liability under the Tax Covenant shall not exceed [●]% of the Consideration; *[to be agreed]*;

