**13.3 Mitigation**

The Buyer shall take all reasonable steps to mitigate any Loss in respect of which a Claim may be made.

**13.4 No Double Recovery**

The Buyer shall not be entitled to recover any amount in respect of any Claim to the extent that it has already recovered the same or substantially the same Loss pursuant to any other provision of this Agreement, any other Transaction Document, or any W&I Insurance Policy.

**13.5 Insurance and Third-Party Recoveries**

(a) Where the Buyer has recovered any amount from an insurer or third party in respect of any Loss giving rise to a Claim, such amount (net of reasonable recovery costs) shall reduce the amount of such Claim;

(b) The Buyer shall, at the request and expense of the Seller, take all reasonable steps to enforce any right against an insurer or third party before bringing a Claim against the Seller.

**13.6 Contingent Liabilities**

Where any Claim is in respect of a contingent liability, the Seller shall not be required to make any payment until the contingent liability has become an actual liability and is due and payable.

**13.7 Tax Benefits**

If any payment is made by the Seller in respect of a Claim, and the Buyer (or any Group Company) receives or would receive a Tax benefit as a result of the matter giving rise to the Claim, the amount payable by the Seller shall be reduced by the amount of such Tax benefit.

