## SCHEDULE 6 — COMPLETION ACCOUNTS MECHANISM

*(abbreviated — full mechanics to be agreed)*

### 1. PREPARATION OF COMPLETION ACCOUNTS

**1.1** The Buyer shall prepare, or procure the preparation of, the Completion Accounts (including a statement of Net Debt and Net Working Capital as at the Completion Date) and shall deliver them to the Seller within [60] Business Days of Completion.

**1.2** The Completion Accounts shall be prepared in accordance with: (i) applicable law; (ii) the accounting policies, principles, and practices applied in preparing the Accounts; and (iii) Schedule 6 (Annex A) (*Accounting Principles and Definitions*).

### 2. REVIEW AND OBJECTION

**2.1** The Seller shall have [30] Business Days after receipt of the Completion Accounts to review them and notify the Buyer in writing of any objections (a "**Notice of Objection**").

**2.2** If the Seller fails to deliver a Notice of Objection within the review period, the Completion Accounts shall be deemed to be agreed and final.

**2.3** If the Seller delivers a Notice of Objection, the Parties shall use good faith efforts to resolve the disputed items within [20] Business Days.

### 3. EXPERT DETERMINATION

**3.1** If the Parties fail to resolve any disputed items within the period specified in paragraph 2.3, either Party may refer the unresolved disputed items to an Expert (being an independent chartered accountant appointed by agreement or, failing agreement within [5] Business Days, nominated by the President of the [Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales / applicable body]).

**3.2** The Expert shall act as an expert and not as an arbitrator. The Expert's decision shall be final and binding on the Parties (save in the case of manifest error or fraud).

**3.3** The costs of the Expert shall be borne: (i) equally between the Parties, or (ii) as the Expert may direct in accordance with the relative merits of each Party's position.

### 4. CONSIDERATION ADJUSTMENT

**4.1** Within [5] Business Days of the Completion Accounts becoming final:

(a) If the Consideration calculated by reference to the Completion Accounts exceeds the Estimated Consideration, the Buyer shall pay the difference to the Seller;

(b) If the Consideration calculated by reference to the Completion Accounts is less than the Estimated Consideration, the Seller shall pay the difference to the Buyer.

