## SCHEDULE 7 — TAX COVENANT

### 1. COVENANT TO PAY

**1.1** The Seller covenants with the Buyer to pay to the Buyer an amount equal to any Tax Liability (as defined below) suffered by any Group Company, to the extent that:

(a) such Tax Liability arises in respect of any Event occurring on or before Completion (a "**Pre-Completion Tax Liability**");

(b) such Tax Liability arises in respect of any Straddle Period, to the extent attributable to the pre-Completion portion;

(c) such Tax Liability arises as a result of the Group Company being or having been a member of any Tax group with any member of the Seller's Group;

(d) any Group Company is made secondarily liable for a Tax Liability of a member of the Seller's Group; or

(e) such Tax Liability arises as a result of any transaction between Group Companies and members of the Seller's Group not being conducted on arm's length terms.

**"Tax Liability"** means:

(a) any actual liability of any Group Company to make a payment (or increased payment) of Tax; or

(b) the use or set-off of a Tax Relief that was taken into account in preparing the Accounts (thereby reducing the Tax Liability payable, where the Tax Liability would otherwise have been covered by this Tax Covenant).

### 2. EXCLUSIONS

**2.1** The Seller shall not be liable under the Tax Covenant in respect of any Tax Liability to the extent that:

(a) it was specifically provided for in the Accounts;

(b) it arises as a result of a Post-Completion Action (as defined below);

(c) it arises as a result of a change in law after the Signing Date (including a change in Tax rates);

(d) it arises as a result of any voluntary act or omission of the Buyer or any Group Company after Completion outside the ordinary course of business;

(e) the Buyer was aware of the matter giving rise to the Tax Liability at Signing;

(f) it is subject to limitations in Clause 13; or

(g) it relates to a Tax that is the subject of a specific indemnity agreed between the Parties.

"**Post-Completion Action**" means any act, omission, or transaction carried out by or on behalf of any Group Company or the Buyer after Completion which is not in the ordinary course of business or which the Seller has not approved in writing.

### 3. PROCEDURE FOR TAX CLAIMS

**3.1** If any Group Company receives any notice, assessment, or demand from a Tax Authority in respect of any Tax for which the Seller may be liable under this Tax Covenant, the Buyer shall:

(a) notify the Seller in writing as soon as reasonably practicable (and in any event within [15] Business Days of receipt of the Tax Authority communication);

(b) provide the Seller with copies of all relevant correspondence and documentation;

(c) take such action as the Seller may reasonably request to dispute, appeal, or otherwise deal with the Tax matter, provided the Seller indemnifies the Buyer against all reasonable costs;

(d) not settle or compromise the Tax matter without the Seller's prior written consent (not to be unreasonably withheld or delayed); and

(e) keep the Seller informed of all material developments.

### 4. STRADDLE PERIOD ALLOCATION

**4.1** For any Straddle Period, Tax shall be allocated between the pre-Completion and post-Completion portions as follows:

(a) income Tax and similar items shall be allocated by closing the books of the relevant Group Company as at the Completion Date; and

(b) other Taxes (e.g., property Taxes, annual licence fees) shall be allocated on a time-apportionment basis.

### 5. TAX REFUNDS

**5.1** If any Group Company receives a repayment of Tax from a Tax Authority in respect of a period on or before Completion (to the extent such Tax was not included as an asset in the Accounts), the Buyer shall procure that the relevant Group Company pays such refund to the Seller promptly after receipt (net of any Tax on such refund and reasonable costs of recovery).

